  "answer": "The charge is **TX-0401**: EUR 240.00 to TechMart Online on 2026-07-20, card payment, status settled.\n\nThere is also **TX-0402**: EUR 240.00 to TechMart Online on 2026-07-14, card payment, status settled. Two identical amounts to the same merchant about a week apart may be a duplicate charge, but I can't tell that from the transaction list alone.\n\nTo open a dispute, I need to know which reason fits:\n\n- **Duplicate charge:** you were billed twice for the same purchase. This would apply if TX-0401 and TX-0402 are for one order.\n- **Goods not received:** you paid but did not receive the item.\n- **Service not rendered:** you paid for a service that was not provided.\n- **Unauthorised debit or card-not-present fraud:** you did not make or authorise the payment.\n\nOnce you tell me which applies, I'll check eligibility first. I'll only open the dispute if that check passes, and I'll confirm the details with you before filing.",
